1
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:06,700
Ryo-san, speaking of which, it's almost

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:12,060
And then there's March 14th, White Day or whatever they call it.
That's just

3
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,770
No, that's not it,

4
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,560
March 13th is Sandwich Day.

5
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,860
Sandwich Day?

6
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:21,260
Look, there's a 1 sandwiched
between the 3s, right?

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:25,480
Plus, "San-wich, san-wich,
san-wich," or so they say.

8
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:29,620
Such rubbish! Stop with this
"what day is today" nonsense!

9
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:41,140
When you watch TV, brighten the room
and sit back from the screen, okay?

10
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:54,420
Anyone without money,
come on over to my place.

11
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:59,000
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,340
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

13
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:12,760
Somehow or other,
it'll all work out eventually.

14
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:29,980
Anyone without work, come to me.

15
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:34,540
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

16
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:38,580
Look, it's burning!

17
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:42,000
Hagaremu too.

18
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:48,280
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

19
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,580
You understand, right?

20
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:53,560
I know, I know.

21
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,860
Follow me!

22
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:13,120
To my dear older brother,

23
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:21,180
Ryo-san!

24
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,800
Mr. Fujita.

25
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:23,500
Hello.

26
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:23,740
Hello.

27
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,800
Hello. Is Ryo-san here?

28
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,860
He's eating in the back.

29
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:31,140
Alright.
Wow, it's really warmed up, hasn't it?

30
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,140
Ryo-san, open up.

31
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:38,080
Geez, I'm in the middle of eating!

32
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,660
Shut up, you annoying guy.

33
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:42,240
Ryo-san,
you can't be eating ramen right now!

34
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,440
It finally arrived from America.

35
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:47,020
The photos of that fined beauty.

36
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,580
No way, really?

37
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:52,560
It's true! And it's the genuine article,
totally uncensored.

38
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,260
They're huge, you know.

39
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,060
Sorry.

40
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,140
Alright, hurry up and show me.

41
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,720
What's this, a jigsaw puzzle?

42
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:07,380
And it's 2,000 pieces.

43
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:11,660
If we import it straight,
customs will stop it, won't they?

44
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:15,860
Did they make it a jigsaw to
slip through the net of the law?

45
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,080
Anyway, let's hurry and put it together.

46
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,500
I also bought the frames.

47
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:24,280
She's quite a beauty, isn't she?

48
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,560
Right? Right?

49
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:28,520
This is great.
Being teased like this really gets to me.

50
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,220
Ryo-chan.

51
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,060
What is it? You could at least knock.

52
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:35,020
You're the one acting all sneaky.

53
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:38,100
We were discussing
America's economic problems.

54
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,400
Anyway, what is it?

55
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,200
It's a phone call for you,
from your younger brother.

56
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,420
From Kinjirō.

57
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,240
Big brother.

58
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,140
Keiko's labor pains have started.

59
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:53,880
So I've been trying to
reach Mom to come over,

60
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:55,760
but I can't get through at all.

61
00:03:56,540 --> 00:04:00,000
Honestly, what are those idiot
spouses doing at such an important time?

62
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,261
Got it,

63
00:04:01,311 --> 00:04:04,620
I'll take her there no matter what,
so don't worry.

64
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:05,720
See you.

65
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,140
What's wrong?

66
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,040
Well, Kinjirō's wife
is about to have a baby.

67
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,740
Is that so?

68
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,580
So Ryo-chan is going to become an uncle!

69
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:17,682
Well, yeah,

70
00:04:17,732 --> 00:04:21,320
so I'm finally going to
have a nephew or niece!

71
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:25,300
Our relatives have been nothing but old geezers and hags,
you know.

72
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,300
A fresh new life is nice, isn't it?

73
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:30,240
The birth of a new life

74
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:32,160
Ryo-san, Ryo-san, come on, hurry up!

75
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:35,720
What is it?
I was enjoying a moment of deep emotion!

76
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,820
Just hurry up already!

77
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:39,660
Look, Ryo-san.

78
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:43,000
The pai-ottsu is almost finished!

79
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:52,360
Isn't it amazing? Looking at yourself like that objectively,
you seem like the lowest, most empty kind of person.

80
00:04:52,880 --> 00:05:00,260
What, mass production? Doesn't look like it. Fine, I'll do it myself.
As an uncle, I don't want to show a sight like this.

81
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,460
No time for that kind of talk.

82
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:04,920
Eeeeeeh!

83
00:05:07,648 --> 00:05:10,060
Not home

84
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:14,000
We could get the seal approved,
but what is that idiot couple doing?

85
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,220
Hey! I'm heading to the family home!

86
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:21,760
Whoa! Amazing!
One more step and it's complete!

87
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,680
W-what!? Let's see, let's see!?

88
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:26,220
Oh! T-this is!

89
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,520
BAN! BAN! BAN! Isn't it!

90
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,260
Alright! I'll help too!

91
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,820
Wait, don't touch it... th-this...

92
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:35,560
It feels oddly familiar.

93
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:38,400
What are you talking about? Hurry, hurry.

94
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:42,080
Y-yeah, then the last two pieces...

95
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,320
There, done!

96
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,200
T-this is...

97
00:05:58,640 --> 00:05:59,780
Just as I thought.

98
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,780
It's a newhalf!

99
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:05,920
Bringing something this
outrageous on a sacred day!

100
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,500
Looks like nobody's home.

101
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,480
Where the hell has he been wandering off to?

102
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,680
Kankichi, what are you doing?

103
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:20,580
Even if you came to steal money,
there isn't a single penny here.

104
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,480
Don't talk nonsense.

105
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,480
Where were you, anyway?

106
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,160
I was on a neighborhood trip to Atami.

107
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:29,580
Those two really are a carefree couple.

108
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:30,600
What did you say?

109
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:34,260
What are you loafing around here for?

110
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:35,520
That's right.

111
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,580
Kinjirō's wife is about to have their baby,

112
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,960
and he wants Mom to come over.

113
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,360
What was that?

114
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,400
Well, that's a big deal!

115
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:45,520
Keep an eye on my things, will you?

116
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,080
You plan to run all the way to the hospital?

117
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:52,020
I'll drive you there in my car.

118
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:56,440
How unlike me.

119
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,383
You're the one giggling like that, you know.

120
00:06:58,433 --> 00:07:01,560
You're about to become a grandma,
so pull yourself together.

121
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:04,220
I don't want to hear that from you.

122
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,640
What? I'm only telling the truth.

123
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:10,100
Now, now, let's hurry.
Come on, please get in.

124
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:11,440
Sorry about this.

125
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,920
Have the contractions stopped?

126
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:19,580
Yes.

127
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,774
You'll have a few more contractions.

128
00:07:22,824 --> 00:07:26,320
They get closer together little by little.

129
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:29,440
When the contractions start again,
please call us.

130
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,600
Yes, thank you for your hard work.

131
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,560
Did you reach your mother?

132
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:37,600
Yeah, my brother just called.
She's on her way here.

133
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,420
That's good.

134
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:39,880
Right.

135
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:43,660
This.

136
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,740
A charm?

137
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,860
It's a charm that brought me happiness.

138
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:54,060
If you carry it too,
I'm sure you'll have a healthy baby.

139
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:57,860
So what kind of happiness did it bring you?

140
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,960
It's a long story.

141
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,260
Please, tell me.

142
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:06,400
Well, it was when I
was in elementary school.

143
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,100
This is serious!

144
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:12,960
Go on, go on!

145
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:20,480
Did someone bully you?

146
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,840
I'll help you, so stop crying.

147
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,040
You need to become stronger, you know.

148
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:35,600
I have no strength and I'm bad at fighting,
so I always get picked on.

149
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:41,000
I want to get stronger, but I'm slow, too.

150
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,920
Big brother is against violence.

151
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,760
But you just told me to get stronger.

152
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,260
Strength isn't just about physical power.

153
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:50,760
It's the strength to not give up.

154
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:53,720
Among animals, the strongest wins,

155
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,840
but humans are different.

156
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:57,920
Humans can talk things
out with each other, right?

157
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:02,560
Talking things through is what matters most.

158
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:05,900
What do you do, mister?

159
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,000
I'm a lawyer.

160
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,760
A lawyer?

161
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:08,260
Mm.

162
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,080
By talking things through,

163
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,860
you can help people

164
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:14,600
and protect them too. That's the work I do.

165
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,120
Wow.

166
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:20,540
Silhouetted against the setting sun,
that person had a very gentle smile.

167
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,940
And that encounter decided my whole life.

168
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,300
Whoa, here they come!

169
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,680
Take this, you villains!

170
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:30,860
The villains are moving!

171
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:31,600
We're not done yet!

172
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,900
Whoa, we're cornered!

173
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,100
Fine, we surrender!

174
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,120
We're not done yet!

175
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,000
We're not done yet!

176
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:37,800
We're not done yet!

177
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,220
We're not done yet!

178
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:39,240
We're not done yet!

179
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:42,420
That's it, hands up!

180
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:45,440
Could you play your toy gun games outside?

181
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:49,060
The setup is that we've
burst into the enemy's hideout!

182
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:51,020
So it's indoor combat, see.

183
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:54,620
Mom, please be a little more careful.

184
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:57,900
Kinjirō, stop studying all
the time and come play with us!

185
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:01,320
If you just keep studying,
you'll get all out of shape.

186
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,440
Yeah, you idiot.

187
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:05,100
Then I'll go outside.

188
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,040
Hang on a sec!

189
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:07,520
Yes.

190
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,820
Use this mikan crate as a desk.

191
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:11,940
There's a mat, too!

192
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:20,100
What a setup! I never thought
you'd actually study outside.

193
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,900
Let us join in, too!

194
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:22,480
Let us play...

195
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:25,180
This isn't playing house, you know!

196
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,240
Okay, okay, I get it.

197
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:34,140
Dinner's almost ready, Daddy.
It's dinnertime!

198
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:34,800
Here you go.

199
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:37,080
Somehow I just can't settle down.

200
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:44,980
Perfect fit.

201
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,900
So you're finally in
junior high Makes me blush.

202
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,180
You finally look like an older brother.

203
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:54,260
Now that you're in junior high,
big brother, please stop picking on me.

204
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:57,140
Of course not. I'm practically an adult now.

205
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,040
Figures.

206
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,140
Thank goodness.

207
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:07,880
So my brother entered junior high,
and guess what happened to me?

208
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,600
As usual, my big brother picked on me.

209
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,060
What an outrageous older brother, right?

210
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,660
Did you catch a cold or something?

211
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:25,640
Idiots don't catch colds.

212
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,380
What's this?

213
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:30,440
Never mind that, can't something
be done about this traffic jam?

214
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:37,080
Keiko must be feeling so anxious,
don't you think?

215
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,320
Well, there's no choice.

216
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:42,600
Let's do this.

217
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,300
Turn into that alley there.

218
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,440
No way,
we can't fit through such a narrow place.

219
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,180
Just leave it to me.

220
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:52,380
S-senpai, watch out, watch out, watch out!

221
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,140
Alright, here we go, full speed!

222
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:56,340
Senpai, please stop!

223
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:00,760
Whoa, dangerous, dangerous, dangerous!

224
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,140
Nakagawa, reverse!

225
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,900
Whoa, what are you doing?

226
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:09,380
Ugh, shortcut, shortcut!

227
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,220
N-no need to rush that much!

228
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:14,880
Ryo-san's insanely dangerous!

229
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:18,480
Hang on, my nephew and niece are -

230
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:21,000
Uncle's coming right now!

231
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:35,440
What? You're going to
a national junior high?

232
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,600
I decided after talking it
over with my teacher, too.

233
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:45,540
I want to gain lots of knowledge
and become a lawyer in the future.

234
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:50,580
Are you an idiot? What's the
point of deciding your future now?

235
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,480
You can only play while you're a kid!

236
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,600
You should only be thinking about playing!

237
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:58,400
Once you're an adult, everyone has to work!

238
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:01,840
Big brother, it seems like you're still
playing even though you're an adult.

239
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,300
What?

240
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:04,020
Yeah, I can't argue with that.

241
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,760
Mind your own business!

242
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,460
Stop it, Kankichi!

243
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:15,080
But going to a school in the education
district costs transportation money, right?

244
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:17,400
I'll get a part-time job myself.

245
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:21,700
Look, why don't you go to the same junior high as him,
Kinjirō?

246
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:22,420
But...

247
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:27,220
Going to the same school as your big brother is what brotherly duty is,
isn't it?

248
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,320
That's impossible.

249
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:31,900
Dad, Mom, please.

250
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,560
Please let me take the
entrance exam. Please.

251
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:42,640
He's serious. What are we going to do, dear?

252
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,660
What choice do we have?

253
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:50,700
I think the national school will be hard,
but if it's just taking the exam, well...

254
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:55,060
Yay, thanks, Dad and Mom!

255
00:13:57,160 --> 00:14:02,360
Well, compared to that idiot Kankichi,
Kinjirō is a hundred times smarter.

256
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,560
Dad.

257
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,820
Just do your best.

258
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,480
That's the tenacity
you'd expect from Kinjirō.

259
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:13,560
Because I really wanted to become a lawyer.

260
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,440
Hey, do you know about the
Kappa Tokyo citizen badge?

261
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:25,200
Yes, I think if you show that, you can use Tokyo's public
facilities and buses for free on Tokyo Citizens' Day, right?

262
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:25,880
Mm.

263
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,720
Here it comes!

264
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,680
Here, the Kappa badge.

265
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,780
But, you know,

266
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,100
the officially sanctioned

267
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:45,780
Kappa badge.

268
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,760
It's not a fake like last year, is it?

269
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:52,780
Do you remember?

270
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:56,300
Oh no, it's the same driver as last year!

271
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:57,660
Shimauchi's cramped, isn't it.

272
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,760
But this year, it's the real thing.

273
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:02,460
Alright.

274
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,920
Then let's get off at Hongō Sanchōme next,

275
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,900
and transfer to the number 16 line.

276
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,080
We could play with this all day.

277
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,720
Hey, what is it, Kankichi?

278
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:22,700
So that's the national school?

279
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:24,100
Yeah, that's right.

280
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,280
So what about it?

281
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,820
Kinjirō's taking the exam there.

282
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,000
Kin-chan's taking the exam here?

283
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:30,940
Wow, that's amazing.

284
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:39,700
He's a bookworm, so he gets good grades at school too.
But this is the place where only the smartest kids from all of Tokyo's 23 wards take the exam, right?

285
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:44,360
I'm definitely going to fail, aren't I?
There's no way I can get in.

286
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,480
I don't think you'll make it.

287
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:56,300
My big brother kept getting in the way of my studying,
and then, the day before the exam...

288
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,440
Kinjirō, you're still up?

289
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,620
I can't sleep.

290
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:10,140
Knock it off already.
You'll make yourself sick.

291
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:13,040
Just leave me alone!

292
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:15,620
Ouch.

293
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,120
Tonight's the crunch time.

294
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:21,000
I'm only worried about your health,
you know.

295
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:24,880
Then leave me alone. You're in the way when you're here,
big brother.

296
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:28,080
Fine, fine. Do whatever you want.

297
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:33,860
Where's big brother?

298
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,160
He went off somewhere early this morning.

299
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,540
Are you okay, hardly getting any sleep?

300
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:39,620
I'm fine.

301
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,500
Well, I'm off then.

302
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:43,840
Good luck, you hear?

303
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,700
Take care.

304
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:48,860
I studied so hard,
but I guess it's hopeless after all.

305
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,160
This should let me give up for good.

306
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:55,440
Guess I'll get some more sleep.

307
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,140
I'm getting nervous already.

308
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,400
There's been an accident
on the Toden tracks.

309
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:16,840
It's not moving anymore.

310
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:19,360
This is bad.

311
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:24,820
It took us so long to
get to Yoshijima Tenjin.

312
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:26,820
Hopefully we can catch up to the Toden.

313
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:28,920
What?

314
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:33,600
Kinjirō!

315
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:37,140
Big brother, the Toden had an accident...

316
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,640
Hurry up and get on the back!

317
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:42,160
But I don't know the way to school.

318
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,420
Just get on!

319
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:44,180
Okay.

320
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:47,180
I know the way to school.

321
00:17:47,180 --> 00:17:48,200
Wait, how?

322
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,360
Hold on tight! Let's go!

323
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:02,320
Alright, at this pace we'll make it in time.

324
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:07,000
Good. Let's check the exam admission ticket.

325
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,560
The exam ticket...

326
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,780
Big brother, stop!

327
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:13,660
What is it?

328
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:14,840
The exam ticket flew away!

329
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:15,280
What?

330
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:21,080
Over there!

331
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,800
I can't take the exam without that!

332
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,940
Sure enough, which way did it go?

333
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,320
Ah!

334
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,780
Big brother!

335
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,720
Wait there, Kinjirō!

336
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,140
Stretcher!

337
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:37,980
Big brother!

338
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,000
He jumped in!

339
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:41,760
In this cold,
what a reckless junior high schooler!

340
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,480
Where is he?

341
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:45,720
He's not here!

342
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,720
Big brother...

343
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,160
Is that you, Matsu-san?

344
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:55,720
Big brother...

345
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,040
Big brother...

346
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:11,060
Big bro

347
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,820
Are you okay? You're something else.

348
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:18,200
Here's your admission ticket.
Don't lose it again.

349
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:18,960
Yeah.

350
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:20,800
Th-thanks

351
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,080
Big bro

352
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,960
Never mind thanks, just hurry and get on.

353
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,200
Right.

354
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:32,520
It got a little wet, though.

355
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:35,640
A good luck charm for passing.

356
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:39,020
Kinjirō, have confidence.

357
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:40,520
Big bro

358
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,180
You'll definitely pass. I believe in you.

359
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:46,400
Big bro

360
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:52,700
Idiot, cry after you've passed.

361
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:58,120
Come on,
we're really going to be late. Get on!

362
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:09,840
Thanks to that,
I was able to pass that junior high too.

363
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,060
What a good big brother.

364
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:16,300
Yeah, he was always fighting with me, but

365
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:19,560
he was the one who
worried about me the most.

366
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,520
If a lovely charm like this protects me,

367
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:25,920
I'm sure I'll be able
to have a healthy baby.

368
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,680
I'm coming in.

369
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,420
Yo.

370
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:34,300
Not ready yet?

371
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:36,800
Big brother.

372
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,480
We were just talking about you.

373
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:42,280
You were probably badmouthing me again,
weren't you?

374
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:45,520
Is Keiko all right?

375
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:48,320
Sorry for calling you over, Mother.

376
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,520
I was off on a leisurely trip,
so I got here late.

377
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:56,280
Well, Mom's here now, so she'll be fine.

378
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:58,060
Thank you, Father.

379
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:04,260
What's that? That's an exam-passing charm!

380
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:08,540
The safe-delivery charm is this one.

381
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:10,600
That's a Suitengū charm!

382
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:13,400
For Kankichi,
you're pretty thoughtful, aren't you?

383
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,400
Well, yeah.

384
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:17,840
So that means the charm on your side

385
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:23,420
brother, since we're both going
into the delivery with charms.

386
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,680
I see.

387
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,620
Thanks, big brother.

388
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,600
Looks like it's starting again.

389
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:31,420
Kinjirō!

390
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:33,420
Yeah, I'll go get the doctor.

391
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:37,040
Keiko, you have to hang in there.

392
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:38,280
Yes.

393
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:47,220
Taking a while

394
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,960
It takes time because it's a childbirth,
you know.

395
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:51,480
Kinjirō-kun.

396
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:55,940
Mom and Dad,
I'm sorry for making you come all this way.

397
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:58,160
Kinjirō-kun, how's the practice?

398
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:00,600
I think it should be just about time now.

399
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,260
It's been a while, hasn't it.

400
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:04,460
Likewise, it's been too long.

401
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,980
Born!

402
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:12,120
She was born safely.

403
00:22:12,620 --> 00:22:13,300
Thank goodness.

404
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:16,840
Nurse, boy or girl?

405
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:18,240
It's a little girl.

406
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,340
A girl?

407
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,280
What is it, Dad?

408
00:22:22,280 --> 00:22:25,720
As long as she's healthy, what's the
difference between a boy and a girl?

409
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:26,875
Well, you know,

410
00:22:26,925 --> 00:22:30,140
they say daughters take
after their fathers, so...

411
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,380
For the father, you know.

412
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:36,320
What is it, big brother?

413
00:22:38,340 --> 00:22:41,480
It's Mom's cute little baby.

414
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,720
I see.

415
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,020
Thank goodness, Kinjirō.

416
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:46,820
Banzai!

417
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:53,420
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

418
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,380
Banzai!

419
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:02,260
Kinjirō, that's great.
You've got to raise her properly.

420
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:09,120
Kan-chan!

421
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:11,860
Yo, everyone from the
neighborhood association!

422
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:15,660
Gin-san told me. It's a girl

423
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:18,860
The young lady must be delighted too,
I'm sure.

424
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:23,340
I brought sake,
so let's get Gin-san and celebrate here.

425
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:25,440
Sounds good, sounds good.

426
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:40,100
They're still partying out in the yard.

427
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:44,380
So many people sincerely congratulating us.

428
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:47,400
This child really is a lucky one.

429
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:50,360
It must be the charm's blessing after all.

430
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:53,220
Yeah, you're right.

431
00:23:58,660 --> 00:24:01,620
Congratulations, congratulations!

432
00:24:01,620 --> 00:24:02,820
Congratulations!

433
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:20,300
Like someone calling out to me,
after the rain.

434
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:27,160
Walking and looking back,
my hand pulled by Gacha.

435
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:34,320
That strange feeling I had back then.

436
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:43,400
So, walking on the tiles of the dawn town,
stepping only on the black ones.

437
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:45,220
Everyone...

438
00:24:47,740 --> 00:24:51,520
Everyone was a child once,

439
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,500
but everyone forgets.

440
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,580
Politicians with their self-important faces,

441
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,940
and aunties with trembling eyebrows too,

442
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:03,940
why not take a turn,

443
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:06,540
around that corner?

444
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:11,700
You'll meet everyone, everyone!

445
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:12,920
Don't go!

446
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:16,380
Over there is Kame-ari,

447
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:19,720
well, surely there's Kame-ari.

448
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:24,880
Everyone, come to our town!

449
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you.

450
00:25:30,940 --> 00:25:33,740
If you weigh giri
against ninjō on the scale,

451
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:36,220
the world of men where giri weighs heavy...

452
00:25:36,220 --> 00:25:39,700
Why am I the one babysitting Kinjirō's kid?

453
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,280
You're really going to leave
your cute grandchild with me?

454
00:25:43,780 --> 00:25:46,500
Next time: "Lullaby of Duty and Humanity."

455
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:47,560
Take care of him!

